STEP D  consequence at the centre-element configuration (exact, all N)
  config:  U_1(x)=(-1)^(x2+x3+x4), U_mu(x)=(-1)^x1 (mu>=2) on an even torus
  => every plaque in the (1,mu) planes equals -1, so a direction-1 link sits in 6
     plaques all equal to -1 and Hess S_W = -(beta/N)*6*(delta/2) = -(3 beta/N) delta.
  (star) at t=0 then requires  Ric_G > (6 beta/N) delta ;  sup_G lam_min(Ric_G) = N/4
  => feasible iff  6 beta/N < N/4  iff  beta < N^2/24.
    SU(2): threshold beta* = N^2/24 = 0.1667 ; deficit at beta=2.5: 15.00x
    SU(3): threshold beta* = N^2/24 = 0.3750 ; deficit at beta=2.5: 6.67x
    SU(4): threshold beta* = N^2/24 = 0.6667 ; deficit at beta=2.5: 3.75x
    SU(5): threshold beta* = N^2/24 = 1.0417 ; deficit at beta=2.5: 2.40x
